{
  "entities": {
    "Customer": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "title": "Customer",
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Represents a customer who uses the services.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the customer."
        },
        "firstName": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "First name of the customer."
        },
        "lastName": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Last name of the customer."
        },
        "email": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Email address of the customer.",
          "format": "email"
        },
        "phone": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Phone number of the customer."
        },
        "address": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Address of the customer."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "firstName",
        "lastName",
        "email",
        "phone"
      ]
    },
    "Ticket": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "title": "Ticket",
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Represents a service request or job ticket.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the ticket."
        },
        "customerId": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Reference to Customer. (Relationship: Customer 1:N Ticket)"
        },
        "serviceType": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Type of service requested (e.g., lawn mowing, golf cart repair)."
        },
        "description": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Detailed description of the service request."
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Current status of the ticket (e.g., open, scheduled, completed)."
        },
        "createdDate": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Date the ticket was created.",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "scheduledDate": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Date the service is scheduled to be performed.",
          "format": "date-time"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "customerId",
        "serviceType",
        "status",
        "createdDate"
      ]
    },
    "Technician": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "title": "Technician",
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Represents a technician who performs the services.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the technician."
        },
        "firstName": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "First name of the technician."
        },
        "lastName": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Last name of the technician."
        },
        "email": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Email address of the technician.",
          "format": "email"
        },
        "phone": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Phone number of the technician."
        },
        "skills": {
          "type": "array",
          "description": "List of skills the technician possesses.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "firstName",
        "lastName",
        "email",
        "phone"
      ]
    },
    "Appointment": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "title": "Appointment",
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Represents a scheduled appointment for a service.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the appointment."
        },
        "ticketId": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Reference to Ticket. (Relationship: Ticket 1:N Appointment)"
        },
        "technicianId": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Reference to Technician. (Relationship: Technician 1:N Appointment)"
        },
        "startTime": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Start time of the appointment.",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "endTime": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "End time of the appointment.",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "notes": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Any notes related to the appointment."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "ticketId",
        "technicianId",
        "startTime",
        "endTime"
      ]
    },
    "Invoice": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "title": "Invoice",
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Represents an invoice for a completed service.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the invoice."
        },
        "ticketId": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Reference to Ticket. (Relationship: Ticket 1:1 Invoice)"
        },
        "amount": {
          "type": "number",
          "description": "Total amount of the invoice."
        },
        "invoiceDate": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Date the invoice was issued.",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "dueDate": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Date the invoice is due.",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "paymentStatus": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Payment status of the invoice (e.g., paid, unpaid, overdue)."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "ticketId",
        "amount",
        "invoiceDate",
        "dueDate",
        "paymentStatus"
      ]
    },
    "Equipment": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "title": "Equipment",
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Represents a piece of equipment owned by a customer.",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Unique identifier for the equipment."
        },
        "customerId": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Reference to Customer. (Relationship: Customer 1:N Equipment)"
        },
        "model": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Model of the equipment."
        },
        "serialNumber": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Serial number of the equipment."
        },
        "engineHours": {
          "type": "number",
          "description": "Engine hours of the equipment."
        },
        "lastServicedDate": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Last date the equipment was serviced.",
          "format": "date-time"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "customerId",
        "model",
        "serialNumber"
      ]
    },
    "Lead": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "title": "Lead",
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Represents a potential customer or opportunity.",
      "properties": {
        "name": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Name of the lead."
        },
        "phone": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Phone number of the lead."
        },
        "email": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Email address of the lead.",
          "format": "email"
        },
        "initialMessage": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The first message or inquiry from the lead."
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Current status of the lead (e.g., New, Qualified, Converted)."
        },
        "source": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Where the lead came from (e.g., Website, Facebook, Missed Call)."
        },
        "createdAt": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Timestamp when the lead was created."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "name",
        "status",
        "createdAt"
      ]
    }
  },
  "auth": {
    "providers": [
      "password",
      "anonymous"
    ]
  },
  "firestore": {
    "structure": [
      {
        "path": "/customers/{customerId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Customer",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Customer"
          },
          "description": "Stores customer profiles. Root-level collection.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "customerId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the customer."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/customers/{customerId}/tickets/{ticketId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Ticket",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Ticket"
          },
          "description": "Stores service tickets for each customer.  Owned by customer identified by customerId.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "customerId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the customer."
            },
            {
              "name": "ticketId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the ticket."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/technicians/{technicianId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Technician",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Technician"
          },
          "description": "Stores profiles for technicians. Root-level collection.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "technicianId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the technician."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/customers/{customerId}/tickets/{ticketId}/appointments/{appointmentId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Appointment",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Appointment"
          },
          "description": "Stores appointments scheduled for each ticket. Owned by ticket, which is owned by customer.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "customerId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the customer."
            },
            {
              "name": "ticketId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the ticket."
            },
            {
              "name": "appointmentId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the appointment."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/customers/{customerId}/tickets/{ticketId}/invoices/{invoiceId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Invoice",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Invoice"
          },
          "description": "Stores invoices for completed services. Owned by ticket, which is owned by customer.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "customerId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the customer."
            },
            {
              "name": "ticketId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the ticket."
            },
            {
              "name": "invoiceId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the invoice."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/customers/{customerId}/equipment/{equipmentId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Equipment",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Equipment"
          },
          "description": "Stores equipment owned by each customer.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "customerId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the customer."
            },
            {
              "name": "equipmentId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the equipment."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "path": "/leads/{leadId}",
        "definition": {
          "entityName": "Lead",
          "schema": {
            "$ref": "#/backend/entities/Lead"
          },
          "description": "Stores potential customer leads. Root-level collection.",
          "params": [
            {
              "name": "leadId",
              "description": "Unique identifier for the lead."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": "The Firestore structure is designed to support the core features of MowerFlow, focusing on simplicity, security, and scalability. It leverages path-based ownership and denormalization to ensure authorization independence and efficient data retrieval. The structure is optimized for mobile use by technicians in the field, aligning with the application's phone-first approach.\n\nAuthorization Independence:\nCustomer data is stored under `/customers/{customerId}`. Each ticket is created as a subcollection under the customer's document (`/customers/{customerId}/tickets/{ticketId}`). This ensures that each ticket inherits the customer's context without requiring complex `get()` calls in security rules. Similarly, appointments and equipment are structured as subcollections under their respective parent documents (ticket and customer). The `technicians` collection is kept separate for managing technician profiles and skills. Leads are stored in a separate root-level collection `/leads` because they do not have an owner until they are converted to a customer.\n\nQAPs (Rules are not Filters):\nThe structure enables secure list operations (QAPs) by segregating data based on ownership. Listing tickets, appointments, or equipment is always scoped to a specific customer or technician, preventing the need for filtering based on document content in the security rules. For technician-specific data, the structure avoids mixing data with different access needs in the same collection by using path-based ownership, which ensures a homogeneous security posture.\n\nThis approach ensures that security rules can be simple and efficient, focusing on path-based authorization (e.g., `request.auth.uid == userId` for customer-owned data) rather than complex data-based filtering. The Invoice documents are also structured as subcollections for each ticket. This is because the Invoice has a 1:1 relationship with the Ticket, and the invoice data is also secured under customer's data."
  }
}
    